-- gate: reject
-- defect: a module lists a value in `exposing (…)` that it never defines
-- rust: reject [E1015] unknown export, reported at the exposing clause
--
-- Found 2026-09-25 (v0.25.19). A module kept `decode` in its `exposing` list
-- after the function was deleted. The dangling name was still published, so a
-- caller's `M.decode body` resolved to a definition that did not exist: the
-- checker gave it a fresh type variable, lowering emitted `any(nil)` for the
-- function value, and the program panicked with `NilDereference` the first
-- time the call ran. An if-it-compiles-it-works break.
module Main exposing (decode, main)

import Sky.Core.Prelude exposing (..)
import Std.Log exposing (println)


main =
    println "x"
